 "description": "<p>Peel Region, together with our contractor I2S, have created this map to inform the public facing Instant App: Smoke Testing in Peel Region. It lets residents search their address and see where smoke testing is happening in their community.&nbsp;</p><p>Smoke testing is part of Peel Region's Downspout Disconnection Program. This program helps reduce the risk of flooding by finding stormwater that may be leaking into the sanitary sewer system which might cause it to overflow. Smoke testing is a simple, safe and cost-effective way to find areas that need imporvement in our sanitary system.&nbsp;</p><p>During smoke testing, field crews blow smoke into sewers then monitor where the smoke exits. The smoke travels through the system to reveal cracks, rooftop stack vents, and any improperly connected downspouts that need to be disconnected. During heavy rainstorms, rainwater entering the sanitary sewer system can add extra water to the system and increase the risk of flooding. Downspouts found connected to the sanitary sewer will be identified and only those property owners will be contacted to participate in the Peel Region’s Downspout Disconnection Program, which completes disconnections of downspouts for residents.</p><p>If smoke testing is scheduled in your neighbourhood, you’ll get a notice in the mail. Once you receive letter notice crews may be working in your area for up to six weeks; however, the actual test along your street typically takes 30 minutes.</p><p>The smoke we use for testing:</p><ul><li>Is odourless</li><li>Is a white, theatrical-style smoke</li><li>Isn't harmful to your health</li><li>Will not harm pets, clothing, draperies or furniture</li><li>Will disappear within minutes</li></ul><p style='margin-bottom:0in;'>&nbsp;</p><p>The Program is rolled out on a neighbourhood-by-neighbourhood basis (called blocks). Blocks with higher priority naturally are started earlier. Blocks are prioritized based on the history of flooding, overflows of sewers to the environment, and sanitary sewer capacity limitations.&nbsp;</p><p>For more information call Peel Region at 905-791-7800, ext. 4409 or visit <a target='_blank' href='https://peelregion.ca/water/wastewater/sanitary-sewer-smoke-testing' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Sanitary sewer smoke testing - peelregion.ca</a></p>",
 "tags": [
  "Peel Region",
  "Smoke Testing",
  "Downspout Disconnection"
 ],
 "snippet": "This map will show smoke testing areas in our Peel Region communities - upcoming (orange) and completed (blue) - to keep residents informed about our ongoing work. Search your address to learn more about when testing is taking place on your street.",
